  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Firdavs is living on planet F. There are NNN cities (numbered 111 through NNN) on this planet; let's denote the value of city iii by viv_ivi​. Firdavs can travel directly from each city to any other city. When he travels directly from city xxx to city yyy, he needs to pay f(x,y)=∣vy−vx∣+y−xf(x, y) = |v_y-v_x|+y-xf(x,y)=∣vy​−vx​∣+y−x coins (this number can be negative, in which case he receives −f(x,y)-f(x, y)−f(x,y) coins).\n\nLet's define a simple path from city xxx to city yyy with length k≥1k \\ge 1k≥1 as a sequence of cities a1,a2,…,aka_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_ka1​,a2​,…,ak​ such that all cities in this sequence are different, a1=xa_1 = xa1​=x and ak=ya_k = yak​=y. The cost of such a path is ∑i=1k−1f(ai,ai+1)\\sum_{i=1}^{k-1} f(a_i, a_{i+1})∑i=1k−1​f(ai​,ai+1​).\n\nYou need to answer some queries for Firdavs. In each query, you are given two cities xxx and yyy, and you need to find the minimum cost of a simple path from city xxx to city yyy. Then, you need to find the length of the longest simple path from xxx to yyy with this cost.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N,Q≤2⋅1051 \\le N, Q \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N,Q≤2⋅105",
      "0≤vi≤1090 \\le v_i \\le 10^90≤vi​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "1≤x,y≤N1 \\le x, y \\le N1≤x,y≤N",
      "the sum of NNN in all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105",
      "the sum of QQQ in all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (30 points):**",
      "1≤N,Q≤1,0001 \\le N, Q \\le 1,0001≤N,Q≤1,000",
      "v1&lt;v2&lt;…&lt;vNv_1 \\lt v_2 \\lt \\ldots \\lt v_Nv1​&lt;v2​&lt;…&lt;vN​",
      "the sum of NNN in all test cases does not exceed 5,0005,0005,000",
      "the sum of QQQ in all test cases does not exceed 5,0005,0005,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers v1,v2,…,vNv_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_Nv1​,v2​,…,vN​.\nThe following QQQ lines describe queries. Each of these lines contains two space-separated integers xxx and yyy.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing two space-separated integers ― the minimum cost and the maximum length.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4 2\n4 2 5 7\n2 3\n3 4\n2 1\n1 1\n2 1",
        "output": "4 3\n3 2\n-1 2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: For the first query, there are two paths with cost 444 from city 222 to city 333:\n\n2→1→32 \\rightarrow 1 \\rightarrow 32→1→3: cost (∣4−2∣+1−2)+(∣5−4∣+3−1)=4(|4-2|+1-2)+(|5-4|+3-1) = 4(∣4−2∣+1−2)+(∣5−4∣+3−1)=4, length 333\n2→32 \\rightarrow 32→3: cost ∣5−2∣+3−2=4|5-2|+3-2 = 4∣5−2∣+3−2=4, length 222\n\nAll other paths have greater costs, so the minimum cost is 444. Among these two paths, we want the one with greater length, which is 333."
      }
